<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Terms of Use | SmartRecover</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/home.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/navbar.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/footer.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/info-pages.css">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Poppins:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.2/css/all.min.css">
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('../includes/navbar') %>

  <main class="info-page">
    <div class="info-container">

      <header class="info-hero">
        <span class="info-kicker"><i class="fa-regular fa-file-lines"></i> TERMS OF USE</span>
        <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
        <p class="info-lead">
          These terms set out the rules for using SmartRecover — Lost &amp; Found JDCOEM.
          By creating an account or submitting reports and claims, you agree to use the
          platform honestly, respectfully, and for its intended campus purpose.
        </p>
        <p class="info-meta">
          <i class="fa-regular fa-calendar"></i>
          Effective date: <strong>To be confirmed on publication</strong>
          <span class="info-badge">Project terms — may require college or legal review.</span>
        </p>
      </header>

      <nav class="info-toc info-card" aria-label="Terms of use contents">
        <h2 class="info-toc-title">On this page</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#tu-acceptance">Acceptance and permitted use</a></li>
          <li><a href="#tu-intended">Intended campus use</a></li>
          <li><a href="#tu-accounts">Account accuracy and security</a></li>
          <li><a href="#tu-truthful">Truthful reports and claims</a></li>
          <li><a href="#tu-prohibited">Prohibited conduct</a></li>
          <li><a href="#tu-privacy">Respect for other users' privacy</a></li>
          <li><a href="#tu-found">Handling found belongings</a></li>
          <li><a href="#tu-photos">Photos and personal information</a></li>
          <li><a href="#tu-email">Email notifications</a></li>
          <li><a href="#tu-moderation">Moderation and account restrictions</a></li>
          <li><a href="#tu-availability">Availability and technical limitations</a></li>
          <li><a href="#tu-liability">Limitation of responsibility</a></li>
          <li><a href="#tu-updates">Updates to these terms</a></li>
          <li><a href="#tu-contact">Contact</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <article class="info-card info-prose">

        <section id="tu-acceptance">
          <h2>1. Acceptance and permitted use</h2>
          <p>
            SmartRecover is provided to help the JDCOEM campus community recover lost
            property. By registering, browsing, submitting reports, or filing claims, you
            accept these Terms of Use and the <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
            If you do not accept them, do not use the platform.
          </p>
          <p>
            You may use SmartRecover only for lawful purposes related to campus lost and
            found activity, and only in ways these terms allow.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="tu-intended">
          <h2>2. Intended use by the campus community</h2>
          <p>
            SmartRecover is designed for students, staff, and visitors of the JDCOEM campus.
            Browsing open reports is open to anyone; submitting reports, claims, and issue
            reports requires an account. The platform is not a general marketplace, notice
            board, or advertising channel, and it should not be used for unrelated
            commercial activity.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="tu-accounts">
          <h2>3. Account accuracy and security</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Provide accurate registration details, including your real name and a valid email address.</li>
            <li>Keep your password confidential — you are responsible for activity done through your account.</li>
            <li>Keep your contact number reachable so finders and claimants can reach you during a recovery.</li>
            <li>Notify the support team through <a href="/report-issue">Report an Issue</a> if you believe your account has been misused.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="tu-truthful">
          <h2>4. Truthful reports and claims</h2>
          <p>
            Every report and claim must be honest and accurate. Describe items truthfully,
            report items only if you genuinely lost or found them, and submit claims only for
            items you genuinely believe belong to you. Deliberately false information
            undermines the recovery process for everyone and may lead to restrictions.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="tu-prohibited">
          <h2>5. Prohibited conduct</h2>
          <p>You must not:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Submit fraudulent, exaggerated, or misleading claims or reports</li>
            <li>Impersonate another person or claim to represent someone you do not represent</li>
            <li>Spam the platform with repetitive, irrelevant, or automated submissions</li>
            <li>Harass, threaten, or abuse other users through report text, claims, or contact details</li>
            <li>Post content that is unlawful, offensive, or that invades others' privacy</li>
            <li>Attempt to disrupt, probe, or misuse the service, including bypassing access controls or rate limits</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="tu-privacy">
          <h2>6. Respect for other users' privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Contact details shared through SmartRecover — such as a reporter's mobile number
            shown on an item page — must be used only for legitimate recovery communication.
            Do not collect, store, republish, or misuse other users' personal information.
            The <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> explains what information the
            platform stores and displays.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="tu-found">
          <h2>7. Handling found belongings</h2>
          <p>
            If you find an item, report it accurately and keep it safe. Do not hand an item
            over until you are reasonably satisfied the recipient is the owner — for example,
            by checking unique details only the owner would know. Meet in a busy campus
            location for handovers. SmartRecover provides the platform but cannot verify
            ownership on your behalf or supervise handovers.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="tu-photos">
          <h2>8. Photos and personal information</h2>
          <p>
            Upload only photos you have the right to share, and avoid images that contain
            unrelated people's personal information or sensitive content. Profile and college
            ID photos are used to support campus trust and are stored as private account
            images; item photos are part of the public reporting workflow. Do not include
            passwords, OTPs, or other secrets in any public text field.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="tu-email">
          <h2>9. Email notifications</h2>
          <p>
            SmartRecover sends automatic emails for certain actions — claim submissions and
            found reports linked to lost items. By using the platform you agree to receive
            these transactional notifications at the email address you registered. You are
            responsible for keeping that mailbox accessible. No marketing emails are sent by
            the platform today.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="tu-moderation">
          <h2>10. Moderation and account restrictions</h2>
          <p>
            Reports carry review states (for example, whether a report is open, claimed,
            recovered, or closed, and whether a claim is pending, approved, or rejected).
            Accounts may be restricted or deactivated where a student violates these terms or
            misuses the service. Note that SmartRecover currently has no self-service
            moderation interface for students; review decisions are handled operationally by
            the campus team, and you may be contacted using your registered details.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="tu-availability">
          <h2>11. Availability and technical limitations</h2>
          <p>
            SmartRecover is provided as a campus project. It may be unavailable occasionally
            for maintenance or due to issues with third-party services it relies on (such as
            the database, image hosting, or mail delivery). Features may change, and the
            platform may not be free of errors at all times. No uptime guarantee is given.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="tu-liability">
          <h2>12. Limitation of responsibility</h2>
          <p>
            SmartRecover provides tools for reporting and connecting people; it does not take
            custody of items, verify ownership, or guarantee that a lost item will be
            recovered. You remain responsible for your own reports, claims, handovers, and
            communications made through the platform. To the extent permitted by applicable
            law, the project contributors and the college are not responsible for losses
            arising from misuse of the platform, fraudulent users, or unsuccessful recovery
            attempts. Nothing in these terms limits rights that applicable law does not allow
            you to waive.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="tu-updates">
          <h2>13. Updates to these terms</h2>
          <p>
            These terms may be revised as the platform evolves. The effective date at the top
            of this page will be updated when a revised version is published. Continued use
            of SmartRecover after an update constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="tu-contact">
          <h2>14. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about these terms can be sent to
            <a href="mailto:support@jdlostfound.edu">support@jdlostfound.edu</a> or submitted
            through the <a href="/report-issue">Report an Issue</a> page. For usage guidance,
            see the <a href="/support">Support center</a> and <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>.
          </p>
          <p class="info-note">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i>
            These are project terms for SmartRecover and may require review by the college or
            an appropriate legal adviser. They do not represent institutional policy unless
            formally adopted.
          </p>
        </section>

      </article>

    </div>
  </main>

  <%- include('../includes/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
